      "content": "Avoid using a loose or inaccurate saw, as it can cause the wood to split or tear out. Make sure your saw is sharp and properly calibrated for the specific wood type you're working with, including the joinery design. Additionally, try using a shouldercut on the pins to reduce the likelihood of splintering. This can help to remove a small increment of wood, allowing the rest to nest flush.",
